Package: pjrt.cuda
Title: CUDA Toolkit Libraries for 'pjrt'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Sebastian", "Fischer", , "seb.fischer@tutamail.com", role = c("cre", "aut"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9609-3197")),
    person("Daniel", "Falbel", , "daniel@posit.co", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0143-2392")))
Description: Provides the CUDA 13.3 native libraries required by the CUDA
    PJRT plugin used by the 'pjrt' package (CUDA runtime, cuBLAS, cuDNN,
    CUPTI, NVRTC, cuFFT, cuSOLVER, cuSPARSE, NvJitLink, NCCL, and NVCC). The
    package itself is lightweight; the CUDA components are downloaded as
    NVIDIA's official redistributable binaries from PyPI into a user cache
    directory the first time the package is loaded.
SystemRequirements: Linux on x86_64 or aarch64; an NVIDIA GPU driver at
    runtime.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/r-xla/pjrt.cuda
BugReports: https://github.com/r-xla/pjrt.cuda/issues
Depends:
    R (>= 4.4.0)
Imports:
    tools,
    utils
Encoding: UTF-8
OS_type: unix
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
